          "Volume 1: The Beginning · by lookataslam",
          "At 5:30 AM, a phone on a desk began to scream.",
          "It did not ring politely. It screamed at the exact piercing pitch some engineer, who clearly harboured a personal vendetta against mornings, had engineered to ensure nobody alive could ignore it. A hand shot out from beneath the tangle of blankets, found the glass screen by pure muscle memory, and slapped it into merciful silence.",
          "“Just a little while longer,” Ma’un negotiated with the ceiling.",
          "The ceiling offered no counter-proposal. Neither did his own limbs, which were already swinging over the edge of the mattress. His body knew something his drowsy mind stubbornly refused to admit: he lost this negotiation every single morning of his life.",
          "He shuffled into the bathroom with the posture of an exhausted question mark, running the tap and cupping cold water over his face until his brain finally clocked into reality. Then came wudu—the sharp, icy shock of it waking every nerve, droplets streaming down his forearms to his elbows, grounding him in the quiet stillness before the world stirred. By the time he had pulled a clean shirt over his head, he was nearly a functioning human being.",
          "Through the open window, carried across the cool dawn breeze, the adhan began.",
