          "He looked down at his chest. A blue button-down shirt. Buttoned. Wrong by exactly one diagonal button, pulling the fabric across his collarbone like an origami accident.",
          "“…How did I not notice that?”",
          "“Because you have the spatial awareness of a potato,” Wardah sighed, stepping forward and undoing the buttons with the practised efficiency of a woman who had dressed three children and refused to let one wander into society looking crooked. “This is why I tell you to sleep early.”",
