          "“You are twenty-one years old. Grow up.”",
          "“I’ll consider it,” Ma’un said, raising his chin with immense dignity. “Sometime next decade.”",
          "He snagged a warm slice of toast from the counter and made for the door.",
          "Wardah watched him disappear into the hall with her arms folded, her wooden spatula resting against the pan, wearing the distinct expression of a mother who has just made a monumental decision about someone else’s entire future and intends to inform him of it later. Twenty-one. Steady part-time income at the accounting firm. A heart as soft as warm bread. And a shirt he couldn't find while literally standing inside it.",
          "It was time.",
          "She went to fetch the folder from her dresser.",
          "Meanwhile, Ma’un walked to work the way he tackled every errand before eight in the morning: one earphone loosely in his ear, half his consciousness still nestled beneath his quilt. At the corner outside the pharmacy, where the brick wall met an awkward lamp-post, he took a brisk left turn—and walked directly, shoulder-first, into a girl in a pink abaya.",
          "The collision produced two simultaneous gasps, a rustle of heavy cloth, and an immediate chorus of identical panic.",
          "“Sorr—”",
          "“Sorry! Sorry, sorry, sorry, it’s my fault, I wasn't looking, I'm so sorry—”",
