          "He drew a complete blank. He searched the filing cabinets of his mind; the drawers were entirely bare. Years of devoutly lowering his gaze on campus and avoiding casual small talk had worked so remarkably well that he had literally never compiled any market research.",
          "“I don’t have any preferences,” he confessed at last, his cheeks pinking. “I just… I kept being religious and lowered my gaze, and I never really thought about that kind of stuff.”",
          "“That is so painfully you,” Hana remarked with genuine, wide-eyed respect. “Heart of gold, zero game. But maybe don’t lead with that when we meet them.”",
          "“Alternative proposal,” Dania chimed in from the armchair, tapping her screen. “Darts. We tape the pictures to the wall, big bro throws blindfolded, and whoever he hits, we call.”",
          "“We are not selecting your brother’s life partner with pub games,” Wardah said firmly.",
          "“I already brought the board,” Hana announced, having materialized from the corner holding a bristled dartboard with a faded anime poster taped across its center. “Sorry, Sensei,” she whispered solemnly to the printed villain.",
          "Wardah confiscated the dartboard with the effortless authority of a mother who had seized contrabands from childhood bedrooms for twenty years. “We choose like respectable, civilized believers. With phone calls, polite inquiries, tea, and far too many intrusive questions.” She drew a single folder from beneath the stack and set it squarely in front of Ma’un. “And I’ve already taken the liberty. This family called me twice before I’d even turned off the stove this morning.”",
