          "Ma’un leaned down. “What?”",
          "Dania looked left, looked right, and whispered straight into his ear:",
          "“Are you still a virgin?”",
          "Ma’un’s brain short-circuited. Every drop of blood in his body rushed straight to his cheeks. His water glass tilted, nearly spilling down his shirt, and he shouted at the top of his lungs:",
          "“WHAT?!”",
          "“Shhh! Shut up!” Dania hissed, smacking her hand over his mouth. “Are you crazy?! Why are you screaming?!”",
          "The entire living room stopped.",
          "Abdul looked over his reading glasses. Wardah’s sponge froze mid-plate. Hana stopped stirring with the wooden spoon in the air. Naba stood by the open fridge, holding a bowl of chicken curry in both hands.",
          "Dania instantly slapped on a bright, fake smile, waving her hands at everyone. “Nothing! Just taking out some loud garbage! Keep going!”",
          "She grabbed Ma’un by his collar and dragged him backward into the dark hallway. Ma’un’s socks slid across the tiles while he flailed his arms.",
          "The second they turned the corner out of sight, Dania let go and punched him in the arm.",
          "“Are you nuts?!” she whispered furiously. “Why did you yell like that?!”",
          "“Anyone with ears would yell!” Ma’un gasped, fixing his collar. “Who asks their brother that in the middle of dinner?!”",
          "“Fair point,” Dania said, crossing her arms. “Anyway. Are you?”",
          "Ma’un glared at her. “Why do you even care?!”",
          "“Because I want to know if getting married made you a real man, or if you’re still the same guy who cries when he loses his phone charger.”",
          "“You are my sister!” Ma’un hissed. “I am not discussing my private life with you!”",
          "“Oh, please,” Dania rolled her eyes. “I know every dumb thing you’ve done since the third grade. Stop acting dramatic. Just tell me.”",
          "Ma’un looked down at his socks. His ears were burning hot. “Yes,” he muttered.",
          "“Louder.”",
          "“…Yes. I am.”",
          "Dania looked at him. She didn't laugh. She didn't tease. She just gave him a tired, disappointed look.",
          "“Yeah,” she said flatly. “That sounds like you.” She tilted her head. “Wait. But don't you guys want normal married stuff?”",
          "“Of course I do!” Ma’un whispered, throwing his hands up. “Eventually! But right now, I don’t even know how to talk to her! She lives in my house and she talks to me like an automated answering machine!”",
          "Dania started to make another sarcastic joke, but stopped.",
          "She looked past his shoulder, out toward the kitchen.",
          "Naba was sliding the curry bowl into the fridge with stiff, careful hands. She didn’t laugh at Hana’s jokes. She didn't sit down. She just stood by the counter with her hands folded, waiting for someone to give her another task. In a house as loud and chaotic as theirs, she looked like a shadow trying hard not to be seen.",
          "“She’s really shut down, isn't she?” Dania said, her voice dropping.",
