          "He thought about Naba holding the cold milk carton with shaking fingers. He thought about her rattling off random facts about garden snails just to fill the quiet. He thought about her standing by the window earlier, looking at him with those serious, lonely eyes, asking what love meant.",
          "“Yeah,” he mumbled, his cheeks red. “I do.”",
          "Dania blinked.",
          "Her smirk completely vanished. Her cheeks turned a light pink. For once in her life, she didn't have a comeback ready.",
          "She was the smart older sister who always had an answer for everything. Yet here was her goofy younger brother, actually falling in love with a girl, while she stood in the hallway alone with her arms crossed.",
          "“Right,” Dania muttered, turning her head toward the wall. “Well. Good luck, then.”",
